nd=3D"1910">Packages de structure</strong> : <code data-start=3D"1913" data=
-end=3D"1922">Classes</code>, <code data-start=3D"1924" data-end=3D"1934">P=
ackages</code>, <code data-start=3D"1936" data-end=3D"1948">Components</cod=
e>, etc.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1955" data-end=3D"2035">
<p data-start=3D"1957" data-end=3D"2035"><strong data-start=3D"1957" data-e=
nd=3D"1985">Packages de comportement</strong> : <code data-start=3D"1988" d=
ata-end=3D"2000">Activities</code>, <code data-start=3D"2002" data-end=3D"2=
017">StateMachines</code>, <code data-start=3D"2019" data-end=3D"2029">UseC=
ases</code>, etc.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2036" data-end=3D"2116">
<p data-start=3D"2038" data-end=3D"2116"><strong data-start=3D"2038" data-e=
nd=3D"2063">Packages de relations</strong> : <code data-start=3D"2066" data=
-end=3D"2080">Associations</code>, <code data-start=3D"2082" data-end=3D"20=
99">Generalizations</code>, <code data-start=3D"2101" data-end=3D"2115">Dep=
endencies</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2117" data-end=3D"2191">
<p data-start=3D"2119" data-end=3D"2191"><strong data-start=3D"2119" data-e=
nd=3D"2148">Packages d=E2=80=99infrastructure</strong> : <code data-start=
=3D"2151" data-end=3D"2157">Core</code>, <code data-start=3D"2159" data-end=
=3D"2167">Common</code>, <code data-start=3D"2169" data-end=3D"2190">Auxili=
aryConstructs</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2193" data-end=3D"2224">Chaque package est d=C3=A9fini par=
 :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2225" data-end=3D"2386">
<li data-start=3D"2225" data-end=3D"2296">
<p data-start=3D"2227" data-end=3D"2296">Des <strong data-start=3D"2231" da=
ta-end=3D"2247">m=C3=A9ta-classes</strong> : par exemple <code data-start=
=3D"2262" data-end=3D"2269">Class</code>, <code data-start=3D"2271" data-en=
d=3D"2282">Attribute</code>, <code data-start=3D"2284" data-end=3D"2295">Op=
eration</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2297" data-end=3D"2386">
<p data-start=3D"2299" data-end=3D"2386">Des <strong data-start=3D"2303" da=
ta-end=3D"2316">relations</strong> entre ces m=C3=A9ta-classes : par exempl=
e, une <code data-start=3D"2359" data-end=3D"2366">Class</code> a des <code=
 data-start=3D"2373" data-end=3D"2385">Attributes</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"2388" data-end=3D"2391">
<h3 data-start=3D"2393" data-end=3D"2425">=F0=9F=8E=93 Utilit=C3=A9 du m=C3=
=A9tamod=C3=A8le UML</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2427" data-end=3D"2839">
<li data-start=3D"2427" data-end=3D"2570">
<p data-start=3D"2429" data-end=3D"2570">=E2=9C=85 <strong data-start=3D"24=
31" data-end=3D"2457">Validation automatique</strong> : Un outil UML peut s=
=E2=80=99assurer que vous ne cr=C3=A9ez pas un lien invalide (ex : une d=C3=
=A9pendance entre deux attributs).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2571" data-end=3D"2687">
<p data-start=3D"2573" data-end=3D"2687">=E2=9C=85 <strong data-start=3D"25=
75" data-end=3D"2596">Cr=C3=A9ation d=E2=80=99outils</strong> : Si vous vou=
lez cr=C3=A9er votre propre modeleur UML, vous devez vous baser sur le m=C3=
=A9tamod=C3=A8le.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2688" data-end=3D"2839">
<p data-start=3D"2690" data-end=3D"2839">=E2=9C=85 <strong data-start=3D"26=
92" data-end=3D"2748">G=C3=A9n=C3=A9ration de code / MDA (Model Driven Arch=
itecture)</strong> : Le m=C3=A9tamod=C3=A8le sert de fondation pour transfo=
rmer les mod=C3=A8les en code ou en autre mod=C3=A8le.</p>
</li>
</ul>
