<hr data-start=3D"3194" data-end=3D"3197">
<h3 data-start=3D"3199" data-end=3D"3215">=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F =C3=80 retenir=
</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3217" data-end=3D"3516">
<li data-start=3D"3217" data-end=3D"3282">
<p data-start=3D"3219" data-end=3D"3282">Le <strong data-start=3D"3222" dat=
a-end=3D"3240">m=C3=A9tamod=C3=A8le UML</strong> d=C3=A9finit <strong data-=
start=3D"3249" data-end=3D"3272">ce qui est autoris=C3=A9</strong> dans UML=
.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3283" data-end=3D"3415">
<p data-start=3D"3285" data-end=3D"3415">UML n=E2=80=99est pas simplement u=
n "dessin de bo=C3=AEtes" : chaque =C3=A9l=C3=A9ment respecte une grammaire=
 stricte, d=C3=A9finie par le <strong data-start=3D"3396" data-end=3D"3414"=
>m=C3=A9tamod=C3=A8le UML</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3416" data-end=3D"3516">
<p data-start=3D"3418" data-end=3D"3516">Les outils UML s=C3=A9rieux (comme=
 Enterprise Architect ou Papyrus) utilisent ce m=C3=A9tamod=C3=A8le en inte=
rne.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3518" data-end=3D"3521">
<h2 data-start=3D"3523" data-end=3D"3586">=F0=9F=94=81 Partie 2 : UML et le=
s processus de d=C3=A9veloppement logiciel</h2>
<p data-start=3D"3588" data-end=3D"3751">UML est un <strong data-start=3D"3=
599" data-end=3D"3626">langage de mod=C3=A9lisation</strong>, mais <strong =
data-start=3D"3633" data-end=3D"3653">pas un processus</strong> en soi. Cel=
a signifie qu=E2=80=99il peut =C3=AAtre utilis=C3=A9 <strong data-start=3D"=
3700" data-end=3D"3750">avec n=E2=80=99importe quel processus de d=C3=A9vel=
oppement</strong>.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"3753" data-end=3D"3858">=F0=9F=92=A1 UML est agnostique a=
ux processus=E2=80=A6 mais certains processus l=E2=80=99int=C3=A8grent plus=
 fortement que d=E2=80=99autres.</h3>
<hr data-start=3D"3860" data-end=3D"3863">
<h3 data-start=3D"3865" data-end=3D"3917">=F0=9F=A7=B1 1. UML et le process=
us Waterfall (Cycle en V)</h3>
<h4 data-start=3D"3919" data-end=3D"3956">=F0=9F=93=8C Rappel du processus =
Waterfall</h4>
<p data-start=3D"3958" data-end=3D"4004">Mod=C3=A8le s=C3=A9quentiel, avec =
des phases rigides :</p>
<blockquote data-start=3D"4005" data-end=3D"4076">
<p data-start=3D"4007" data-end=3D"4076"><strong data-start=3D"4007" data-e=
nd=3D"4076">Sp=C3=A9cification =E2=86=92 Conception =E2=86=92 Impl=C3=A9men=
tation =E2=86=92 Tests =E2=86=92 D=C3=A9ploiement</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<h4 data-start=3D"4078" data-end=3D"4105">=F0=9F=8E=AF Usage typique d=E2=
=80=99UML</h4>
<ul data-start=3D"4107" data-end=3D"4425">
<li data-start=3D"4107" data-end=3D"4176">
<p data-start=3D"4109" data-end=3D"4176">Diagramme de <strong data-start=3D=
"4122" data-end=3D"4143">cas d=E2=80=99utilisation</strong> pendant l=E2=80=
=99analyse fonctionnelle.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4177" data-end=3D"4262">
<p data-start=3D"4179" data-end=3D"4262">Diagramme de <strong data-start=3D=
"4192" data-end=3D"4203">classes</strong>, <strong data-start=3D"4205" data=
-end=3D"4219">composants</strong>, et <strong data-start=3D"4224" data-end=
=3D"4239">d=C3=A9ploiement</strong> pendant la conception.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4263" data-end=3D"4343">
<p data-start=3D"4265" data-end=3D"4343">Diagrammes de <strong data-start=
=3D"4279" data-end=3D"4291">s=C3=A9quence</strong> ou <strong data-start=3D=
"4295" data-end=3D"4308">activit=C3=A9s</strong> pour documenter les flux i=
nternes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4344" data-end=3D"4425">
<p data-start=3D"4346" data-end=3D"4425">UML joue un r=C3=B4le <strong data=
-start=3D"4363" data-end=3D"4373">formel</strong> dans la documentation, co=
mme support de validation.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"4427" data-end=3D"4444">=F0=9F=A7=A0 Avantages</h4>
<ul data-start=3D"4446" data-end=3D"4575">
<li data-start=3D"4446" data-end=3D"4509">
<p data-start=3D"4448" data-end=3D"4509">UML cadre bien avec les phases <st=
rong data-start=3D"4479" data-end=3D"4508">s=C3=A9par=C3=A9es et bien d=C3=
=A9finies</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4510" data-end=3D"4575">
<p data-start=3D"4512" data-end=3D"4575">Id=C3=A9al pour des projets r=C3=
=A9glement=C3=A9s (ex : d=C3=A9fense, a=C3=A9rospatial).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4577" data-end=3D"4580">
<h3 data-start=3D"4582" data-end=3D"4642">=E2=9A=99=EF=B8=8F 2. UML et le p=
rocessus RUP (Rational Unified Process)</h3>
<h4 data-start=3D"4644" data-end=3D"4663">=F0=9F=A7=A9 RUP en bref</h4>
<p data-start=3D"4665" data-end=3D"4762">M=C3=A9thodologie it=C3=A9rative, =
orient=C3=A9e objet, fortement coupl=C3=A9e =C3=A0 UML. Elle est divis=C3=
=A9e en 4 phases :</p>
<blockquote data-start=3D"4763" data-end=3D"4816">
<p data-start=3D"4765" data-end=3D"4816">Inception =E2=86=92 Elaboration =
=E2=86=92 Construction =E2=86=92 Transition</p>
</blockquote>
<h4 data-start=3D"4818" data-end=3D"4846">=F0=9F=8E=AF Usage d=E2=80=99UML =
dans RUP</h4>
<ul data-start=3D"4848" data-end=3D"5125">
<li data-start=3D"4848" data-end=3D"5125">
<p data-start=3D"4850" data-end=3D"4908">UML est <strong data-start=3D"4858=
" data-end=3D"4867">natif</strong> =C3=A0 RUP, utilis=C3=A9 pour tous les a=
rtefacts :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4911" data-end=3D"5125">
<li data-start=3D"4911" data-end=3D"4968">
<p data-start=3D"4913" data-end=3D"4968"><strong data-start=3D"4913" data-e=
nd=3D"4948">Diagrammes de cas d=E2=80=99utilisation</strong> pour les exige=
nces.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4971" data-end=3D"5031">
<p data-start=3D"4973" data-end=3D"5031"><strong data-start=3D"4973" data-e=
