<hr data-start=3D"6732" data-end=3D"6735">
<h2 data-start=3D"6737" data-end=3D"6788">=F0=9F=8E=93 Niveau expert : UML =
dans MDA, DevOps et CI/CD</h2>
<ul data-start=3D"6790" data-end=3D"7184">
<li data-start=3D"6790" data-end=3D"6916">
<p data-start=3D"6792" data-end=3D"6916">UML est la <strong data-start=3D"6=
803" data-end=3D"6846">base du Model Driven Architecture (MDA)</strong> : o=
n mod=C3=A9lise en UML, puis on g=C3=A9n=C3=A8re code, bases de donn=C3=A9e=
s, configs.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6917" data-end=3D"7065">
<p data-start=3D"6919" data-end=3D"7065">Dans les pipelines DevOps, certain=
s outils (ex : Papyrus, Modelio) permettent de <strong data-start=3D"7000" =
data-end=3D"7046">g=C3=A9n=C3=A9rer des artefacts UML =C3=A0 partir du code=
</strong> ou <strong data-start=3D"7050" data-end=3D"7064">vice versa</stro=
ng>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7066" data-end=3D"7184">
<p data-start=3D"7068" data-end=3D"7184">UML peut aussi =C3=AAtre utilis=C3=
=A9 pour <strong data-start=3D"7101" data-end=3D"7132">g=C3=A9n=C3=A9rer le=
s tests (TDD/BDD)</strong> via des mod=C3=A8les de comportement (activit=C3=
=A9s, =C3=A9tats).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"7186" data-end=3D"7189">
<h2 data-start=3D"7191" data-end=3D"7207">=F0=9F=A7=A0 Conclusion</h2>
<ul data-start=3D"7209" data-end=3D"7632">
<li data-start=3D"7209" data-end=3D"7363">
<p data-start=3D"7211" data-end=3D"7363">Le <strong data-start=3D"7214" dat=
a-end=3D"7232">m=C3=A9tamod=C3=A8le UML</strong> vous permet de comprendre =
<strong data-start=3D"7259" data-end=3D"7283">la structure interne</strong>=
 d=E2=80=99UML, indispensable pour cr=C3=A9er vos propres outils, extension=
s, ou validations.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7364" data-end=3D"7632">
<p data-start=3D"7366" data-end=3D"7489">UML peut =C3=AAtre utilis=C3=A9 <s=
trong data-start=3D"7388" data-end=3D"7428">dans tout processus de d=C3=A9v=
eloppement</strong>. Son int=C3=A9gration varie selon le degr=C3=A9 de form=
alisme requis :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"7492" data-end=3D"7632">
<li data-start=3D"7492" data-end=3D"7561">
<p data-start=3D"7494" data-end=3D"7561"><strong data-start=3D"7494" data-e=
nd=3D"7514">Waterfall et RUP</strong> : UML joue un r=C3=B4le <strong data-=
start=3D"7534" data-end=3D"7560">structurant et central</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7564" data-end=3D"7632">
<p data-start=3D"7566" data-end=3D"7632"><strong data-start=3D"7566" data-e=
nd=3D"7575">Agile</strong> : UML est utilis=C3=A9 <strong data-start=3D"759=
4" data-end=3D"7631">comme support visuel et adaptatif</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
