<p data-start=3D"464" data-end=3D"566">Le <strong data-start=3D"467" data-e=
nd=3D"492">diagramme de packages</strong> (ou <em data-start=3D"497" data-e=
nd=3D"514">Package Diagram</em>) est un <strong data-start=3D"523" data-end=
=3D"551">diagramme structurel UML</strong> utilis=C3=A9 pour :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"567" data-end=3D"860">
<li data-start=3D"567" data-end=3D"668">
<p data-start=3D"569" data-end=3D"668">Organiser <strong data-start=3D"579"=
 data-end=3D"620">logiquement les =C3=A9l=C3=A9ments d=E2=80=99un syst=C3=
=A8me</strong> (classes, composants, cas d=E2=80=99utilisation, etc.),</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"669" data-end=3D"747">
<p data-start=3D"671" data-end=3D"747">Repr=C3=A9senter des <strong data-st=
art=3D"687" data-end=3D"698">modules</strong>, <strong data-start=3D"700" d=
ata-end=3D"719">espaces de noms</strong> ou <strong data-start=3D"723" data=
-end=3D"746">couches logicielles</strong>,</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"748" data-end=3D"860">
<p data-start=3D"750" data-end=3D"860">Illustrer les <strong data-start=3D"=
764" data-end=3D"792">relations de d=C3=A9pendances</strong>, d=E2=80=99<st=
rong data-start=3D"796" data-end=3D"811">importation</strong>, ou de <stron=
g data-start=3D"819" data-end=3D"833">contenance</strong> entre diff=C3=A9r=
ents packages.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"862" data-end=3D"935">Il est <strong data-start=3D"869" da=
ta-end=3D"895">particuli=C3=A8rement utile</strong> dans les grands syst=C3=
=A8mes pour assurer :</p>
