<hr data-start=3D"4523" data-end=3D"4526">
<h3 data-start=3D"4528" data-end=3D"4576">3.5. Gestion des conflits et sync=
hronisation</h3>
<hr data-start=3D"4578" data-end=3D"4581">
<ul data-start=3D"4583" data-end=3D"5021">
<li data-start=3D"4583" data-end=3D"4881">
<p data-start=3D"4585" data-end=3D"4881"><strong data-start=3D"4585" data-e=
nd=3D"4636">Les joins synchronisent les branches parall=C3=A8les</strong>, =
mais parfois on peut avoir des branches ind=C3=A9pendantes qui ne doivent p=
as bloquer la progression. UML offre des m=C3=A9canismes avanc=C3=A9s (comm=
e les <strong data-start=3D"4779" data-end=3D"4807">n=C5=93uds de synchroni=
sation</strong> plus souples), mais la plupart du temps, le join classique =
est utilis=C3=A9.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4882" data-end=3D"5021">
<p data-start=3D"4884" data-end=3D"5021">Il faut bien concevoir la logique =
m=C3=A9tier pour =C3=A9viter les <strong data-start=3D"4941" data-end=3D"49=
54">deadlocks</strong> (blocages) o=C3=B9 certaines branches attendent ind=
=C3=A9finiment une autre.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"5023" data-end=3D"5026">
<h2 data-start=3D"5028" data-end=3D"5081">4. =C3=89v=C3=A9nements, conditio=
ns et parall=C3=A9lisme combin=C3=A9s</h2>
<hr data-start=3D"5083" data-end=3D"5086">
<h3 data-start=3D"5088" data-end=3D"5119">4.1. Interactions complexes</h3>
<hr data-start=3D"5121" data-end=3D"5124">
<p data-start=3D"5126" data-end=3D"5204">Les processus r=C3=A9els combinent=
 souvent =C3=A9v=C3=A9nements, conditions et parall=C3=A9lisme :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5206" data-end=3D"5414">
<li data-start=3D"5206" data-end=3D"5343">
<p data-start=3D"5208" data-end=3D"5343">Par exemple, on peut lancer plusie=
urs t=C3=A2ches en parall=C3=A8le, chacune pouvant =C3=AAtre interrompue pa=
r un =C3=A9v=C3=A9nement (ex. annulation, erreur)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5344" data-end=3D"5414">
<p data-start=3D"5346" data-end=3D"5414">Ou un =C3=A9v=C3=A9nement d=C3=A9c=
lenche un fork de plusieurs actions conditionn=C3=A9es</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"5416" data-end=3D"5419">
<h3 data-start=3D"5421" data-end=3D"5486">4.2. Mod=C3=A9lisation des interr=
uptions et =C3=A9v=C3=A9nements asynchrones</h3>
<hr data-start=3D"5488" data-end=3D"5491">
<ul data-start=3D"5493" data-end=3D"5730">
<li data-start=3D"5493" data-end=3D"5624">
<p data-start=3D"5495" data-end=3D"5624">UML permet de mod=C3=A9liser des <=
strong data-start=3D"5523" data-end=3D"5551">interruptions de r=C3=A9gions<=
/strong> : une r=C3=A9gion d=E2=80=99activit=C3=A9 peut =C3=AAtre interromp=
ue par un =C3=A9v=C3=A9nement externe</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5625" data-end=3D"5730">
<p data-start=3D"5627" data-end=3D"5730">Exemple : un processus de paiement=
 en parall=C3=A8le peut =C3=AAtre interrompu par un =C3=A9v=C3=A9nement =E2=
=80=9Cpaiement annul=C3=A9=E2=80=9D</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"5732" data-end=3D"5735">
<h3 data-start=3D"5737" data-end=3D"5788">4.3. Boucles parall=C3=A8les avec=
 conditions d=E2=80=99arr=C3=AAt</h3>
<hr data-start=3D"5790" data-end=3D"5793">
<ul data-start=3D"5795" data-end=3D"5958">
<li data-start=3D"5795" data-end=3D"5886">
<p data-start=3D"5797" data-end=3D"5886">Une boucle peut lancer des branche=
s parall=C3=A8les r=C3=A9p=C3=A9t=C3=A9es tant qu=E2=80=99une condition est=
 vraie</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5887" data-end=3D"5958">
<p data-start=3D"5889" data-end=3D"5958">Exemple : traitement parall=C3=A8l=
e de lots de donn=C3=A9es, jusqu=E2=80=99=C3=A0 =C3=A9puisement</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"5960" data-end=3D"5963">
<h2 data-start=3D"5965" data-end=3D"6025">5. Bonnes pratiques pour g=C3=A9r=
er =C3=A9v=C3=A9nements et parall=C3=A9lisme</h2>
<hr data-start=3D"6027" data-end=3D"6030">
<ul data-start=3D"6032" data-end=3D"6573">
<li data-start=3D"6032" data-end=3D"6135">
<p data-start=3D"6034" data-end=3D"6135"><strong data-start=3D"6034" data-e=
nd=3D"6062">Modulariser le diagramme</strong> : d=C3=A9couper les processus=
 complexes en sous-activit=C3=A9s ou sous-processus</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6136" data-end=3D"6218">
<p data-start=3D"6138" data-end=3D"6218"><strong data-start=3D"6138" data-e=
nd=3D"6188">Nommer clairement les =C3=A9v=C3=A9nements et conditions</stron=
g> pour =C3=A9viter toute confusion</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6219" data-end=3D"6299">
<p data-start=3D"6221" data-end=3D"6299"><strong data-start=3D"6221" data-e=
nd=3D"6250">Privil=C3=A9gier la simplicit=C3=A9</strong> : un diagramme tro=
p complexe devient illisible</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6300" data-end=3D"6390">
<p data-start=3D"6302" data-end=3D"6390"><strong data-start=3D"6302" data-e=
nd=3D"6333">Valider les flux parall=C3=A8les</strong> pour =C3=A9viter les =
blocages ou comportements ind=C3=A9sirables</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6391" data-end=3D"6499">
<p data-start=3D"6393" data-end=3D"6499"><strong data-start=3D"6393" data-e=
nd=3D"6420">Utiliser des outils UML</strong> capables de g=C3=A9rer la comp=
lexit=C3=A9 (ex : Enterprise Architect, Visual Paradigm)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6500" data-end=3D"6573">
<p data-start=3D"6502" data-end=3D"6573"><strong data-start=3D"6502" data-e=
nd=3D"6573">Documenter les r=C3=A8gles m=C3=A9tier associ=C3=A9es aux =C3=
=A9v=C3=A9nements et conditions</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"6575" data-end=3D"6578">
