<hr data-start=3D"441" data-end=3D"444">
<h1 data-start=3D"446" data-end=3D"499">=F0=9F=8E=93 Tutoriel UML =E2=80=94=
 Diagramme d=E2=80=99=C3=89tats (State Machine)</h1>
<h2 data-start=3D"501" data-end=3D"540">1. Introduction au diagramme d=E2=
=80=99=C3=A9tats</h2>
<p data-start=3D"542" data-end=3D"733">Le diagramme d=E2=80=99=C3=A9tats en=
 UML (aussi appel=C3=A9 "diagramme d=E2=80=99automate d=E2=80=99=C3=A9tats"=
 ou "state machine diagram") permet de mod=C3=A9liser le <strong data-start=
=3D"666" data-end=3D"709">cycle de vie d=E2=80=99un objet ou d=E2=80=99un s=
yst=C3=A8me</strong>, en se focalisant sur :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"735" data-end=3D"971">
<li data-start=3D"735" data-end=3D"786">
<p data-start=3D"737" data-end=3D"786">Les <strong data-start=3D"741" data-=
end=3D"761">diff=C3=A9rents =C3=A9tats</strong> qu=E2=80=99un objet peut pr=
endre</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"787" data-end=3D"843">
<p data-start=3D"789" data-end=3D"843">Les <strong data-start=3D"793" data-=
end=3D"808">transitions</strong> d=C3=A9clench=C3=A9es par des <strong data=
-start=3D"829" data-end=3D"843">=C3=A9v=C3=A9nements</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"844" data-end=3D"901">
<p data-start=3D"846" data-end=3D"901">Les <strong data-start=3D"850" data-=
end=3D"864">conditions</strong> (ou garde) associ=C3=A9es aux transitions</=
p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"902" data-end=3D"971">
<p data-start=3D"904" data-end=3D"971">Les <strong data-start=3D"908" data-=
end=3D"919">actions</strong> ex=C3=A9cut=C3=A9es =C3=A0 l=E2=80=99entr=C3=
=A9e, =C3=A0 la sortie ou durant un =C3=A9tat</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"973" data-end=3D"1149">Il est id=C3=A9al pour mod=C3=A9lis=
er des <strong data-start=3D"1005" data-end=3D"1040">syst=C3=A8mes =C3=A0 c=
omportement r=C3=A9actif</strong>, comme une porte automatique, un distribu=
teur de billets, un processus m=C3=A9tier ou une entit=C3=A9 m=C3=A9tier co=
mplexe.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1151" data-end=3D"1154">
<h2 data-start=3D"1156" data-end=3D"1183">2. Concepts fondamentaux</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"1185" data-end=3D"1205">2.1 =C3=89tat (State)</h3>
<p data-start=3D"1207" data-end=3D"1364">Un <strong data-start=3D"1210" dat=
a-end=3D"1218">=C3=A9tat</strong> repr=C3=A9sente une <strong data-start=3D=
"1234" data-end=3D"1254">situation stable</strong> dans laquelle un objet s=
e trouve pendant un certain temps, tant qu=E2=80=99aucun =C3=A9v=C3=A9nemen=
t ne le fait changer d=E2=80=99=C3=A9tat.</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"1366" data-end=3D"1384">=F0=9F=9F=A6 Notation :</h4>
<ul data-start=3D"1386" data-end=3D"1605">
<li data-start=3D"1386" data-end=3D"1456">
<p data-start=3D"1388" data-end=3D"1456">Un <strong data-start=3D"1391" dat=
a-end=3D"1423">rectangle aux coins arrondis</strong> avec le nom de l=E2=80=
=99=C3=A9tat au centre.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1457" data-end=3D"1605">
<p data-start=3D"1459" data-end=3D"1477">Il peut contenir :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1480" data-end=3D"1605">
<li data-start=3D"1480" data-end=3D"1533">
<p data-start=3D"1482" data-end=3D"1533">des <strong data-start=3D"1486" da=
ta-end=3D"1506">actions internes</strong> (<code data-start=3D"1508" data-e=
nd=3D"1513">do/</code>, <code data-start=3D"1515" data-end=3D"1523">entry/<=
/code>, <code data-start=3D"1525" data-end=3D"1532">exit/</code>)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1536" data-end=3D"1574">
<p data-start=3D"1538" data-end=3D"1574">des <strong data-start=3D"1542" da=
ta-end=3D"1556">sous-=C3=A9tats</strong> (=C3=A9tats imbriqu=C3=A9s)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1577" data-end=3D"1605">
<p data-start=3D"1579" data-end=3D"1605">des <strong data-start=3D"1583" da=
