un d=C3=A9clenchement de m=C3=A9thode ?</h3>
<p data-start=3D"1270" data-end=3D"1378">Le <strong data-start=3D"1273" dat=
a-end=3D"1304">d=C3=A9clenchement d=E2=80=99une m=C3=A9thode</strong> corre=
spond =C3=A0 l=E2=80=99envoi d=E2=80=99un <strong data-start=3D"1331" data-=
end=3D"1366">message synchrone ou asynchrone</strong> =C3=A0 un objet.</p>
<p data-start=3D"1380" data-end=3D"1399">Dans le diagramme :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1400" data-end=3D"1610">
<li data-start=3D"1400" data-end=3D"1489">
<p data-start=3D"1402" data-end=3D"1489">Ce d=C3=A9clenchement est repr=C3=
=A9sent=C3=A9 par une <strong data-start=3D"1442" data-end=3D"1488">fl=C3=
=A8che horizontale vers une lifeline cible</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1490" data-end=3D"1610">
<p data-start=3D"1492" data-end=3D"1610">Une <strong data-start=3D"1496" da=
ta-end=3D"1518">bande d=E2=80=99activation</strong> (rectangle vertical sur=
 la lifeline) est g=C3=A9n=C3=A9r=C3=A9e, indiquant que l=E2=80=99objet ex=
=C3=A9cute la m=C3=A9thode.</p>
</li>
</ul>
