<hr data-start=3D"340" data-end=3D"343">
<h1 data-start=3D"345" data-end=3D"383">=F0=9F=95=92 Tutoriel UML : Diagram=
me de Temps</h1>
<hr data-start=3D"385" data-end=3D"388">
<h2 data-start=3D"390" data-end=3D"420">=F0=9F=94=B0 1. Introduction g=C3=
=A9n=C3=A9rale</h2>
<p data-start=3D"422" data-end=3D"720">Le <strong data-start=3D"425" data-e=
nd=3D"451">diagramme de temps UML</strong> est un type de <strong data-star=
t=3D"467" data-end=3D"494">diagramme d=E2=80=99interaction</strong> utilis=
=C3=A9 pour mod=C3=A9liser le <strong data-start=3D"521" data-end=3D"564">c=
omportement des objets au fil du temps</strong>. Il est particuli=C3=A8reme=
nt adapt=C3=A9 =C3=A0 la <strong data-start=3D"602" data-end=3D"641">mod=C3=
=A9lisation de syst=C3=A8mes temps r=C3=A9el</strong>, embarqu=C3=A9s, ou n=
=C3=A9cessitant le respect <strong data-start=3D"680" data-end=3D"719">de c=
ontraintes temporelles strictes</strong>.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"722" data-end=3D"748">Objectifs principaux :</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"749" data-end=3D"989">
<li data-start=3D"749" data-end=3D"823">
<p data-start=3D"751" data-end=3D"823">Visualiser le <strong data-start=3D"=
765" data-end=3D"808">changement d=E2=80=99=C3=A9tat des objets ou signaux<=
/strong> dans le temps.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"824" data-end=3D"890">
<p data-start=3D"826" data-end=3D"890">Repr=C3=A9senter <strong data-start=
=3D"838" data-end=3D"889">les d=C3=A9lais, dur=C3=A9es, interruptions et =
=C3=A9v=C3=A9nements</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"891" data-end=3D"989">
<p data-start=3D"893" data-end=3D"989">Fournir une <strong data-start=3D"90=
5" data-end=3D"927">analyse temporelle</strong> pr=C3=A9cise pour la valida=
tion de performances et de contraintes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"991" data-end=3D"994">
<h2 data-start=3D"996" data-end=3D"1048">=F0=9F=A7=B1 2. Concepts fondament=
aux du diagramme de temps</h2>
<hr data-start=3D"1050" data-end=3D"1053">
<h3 data-start=3D"1055" data-end=3D"1080">2.1 Axes du diagramme</h3>
<p data-start=3D"1082" data-end=3D"1149">Le diagramme de temps s=E2=80=99ap=
parente =C3=A0 une <strong data-start=3D"1122" data-end=3D"1147">grille ave=
c deux axes</strong> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1151" data-end=3D"1298">
<li data-start=3D"1151" data-end=3D"1199">
<p data-start=3D"1153" data-end=3D"1199"><strong data-start=3D"1153" data-e=
nd=3D"1171">Axe horizontal</strong> : le <strong data-start=3D"1177" data-e=
nd=3D"1199">temps qui s=E2=80=99=C3=A9coule</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1200" data-end=3D"1298">
<p data-start=3D"1202" data-end=3D"1298"><strong data-start=3D"1202" data-e=
nd=3D"1218">Axe vertical</strong> : les <strong data-start=3D"1225" data-en=
d=3D"1238">lifelines</strong> (lignes de vie) repr=C3=A9sentant des objets,=
 signaux ou entit=C3=A9s</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1300" data-end=3D"1435">Chaque ligne montre <strong data-s=
tart=3D"1320" data-end=3D"1383">comment l=E2=80=99=C3=A9tat ou la valeur d=
=E2=80=99un objet =C3=A9volue dans le temps</strong>, souvent sous forme de=
 <strong data-start=3D"1407" data-end=3D"1434">courbes ou blocs d=E2=80=99=
=C3=A9tat</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1437" data-end=3D"1440">
<h3 data-start=3D"1442" data-end=3D"1473">2.2 Lifeline (ligne de vie)</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1475" data-end=3D"1726">
<li data-start=3D"1475" data-end=3D"1530">
<p data-start=3D"1477" data-end=3D"1530">Repr=C3=A9sente un <strong data-st=
art=3D"1491" data-end=3D"1529">objet, un acteur, ou une ressource</strong>.=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1531" data-end=3D"1647">
<p data-start=3D"1533" data-end=3D"1647">Affich=C3=A9e comme une <strong da=
ta-start=3D"1552" data-end=3D"1573">ligne horizontale</strong>, contraireme=
nt aux autres diagrammes d=E2=80=99interaction o=C3=B9 elle est verticale.<=
/p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1648" data-end=3D"1726">
<p data-start=3D"1650" data-end=3D"1726">Elle montre l=E2=80=99<strong data=
-start=3D"1664" data-end=3D"1699">=C3=A9volution d=E2=80=99un attribut ou =
=C3=A9tat</strong> de l=E2=80=99entit=C3=A9 dans le temps.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1728" data-end=3D"1751">Exemples de lifelines :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1752" data-end=3D"1822">
<li data-start=3D"1752" data-end=3D"1770">
<p data-start=3D"1754" data-end=3D"1770"><code data-start=3D"1754" data-end=
=3D"1770">moteur: Moteur</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1771" data-end=3D"1806">
<p data-start=3D"1773" data-end=3D"1806"><code data-start=3D"1773" data-end=
=3D"1806">capteurTemp: CapteurTemperature</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1807" data-end=3D"1822">
<p data-start=3D"1809" data-end=3D"1822"><code data-start=3D"1809" data-end=
=3D"1822">signalFrein</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1824" data-end=3D"1827">
<h3 data-start=3D"1829" data-end=3D"1863">2.3 Chronologie des =C3=A9v=C3=A9=
nements</h3>
<p data-start=3D"1865" data-end=3D"1894">Les =C3=A9v=C3=A9nements peuvent =
=C3=AAtre :</p>
